WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.685
Least privilege means providing users, devices, applications,

00:00:03.685 --> 00:00:07.320
and services only the access needed to perform authorized functions.

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:11.165
It reduces the amount of unnecessary capability available if an account, device,

00:00:11.165 --> 00:00:12.760
or process is misused.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.560
Zero Trust applies least privilege at the resource level.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:19.050
Instead of granting broad access because a request crossed a network boundary,

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:23.100
policy evaluates whether the requester needs this particular application, service,

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.718
function, or data set.

00:00:24.718 --> 00:00:28.600
Permissions should reflect role and context, but roles alone can become too broad.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:33.160
Organizations may combine job responsibilities with resource attributes, device posture,

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:36.180
risk signals, time, purpose, and approval requirements.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.920
Privileged access deserves stronger governance because administrative actions can affect

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.435
many systems or users.

00:00:41.435 --> 00:00:45.640
Clear ownership, separate administrative roles, appropriate approval, limited duration,

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:48.060
and detailed monitoring can reduce exposure.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.880
Service and workload accounts also require least privilege.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:54.370
Long-lived credentials and broad machine permissions can become invisible operational

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:55.235
dependencies,

00:00:55.235 --> 00:01:00.050
so teams need inventories, ownership, review, and controlled lifecycle management.

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.440
Access is not a one-time design decision.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:06.480
Responsibilities change, projects end, applications retire, and temporary needs expire.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:10.325
Periodic review helps remove access that is no longer justified and confirms that

00:01:10.325 --> 00:01:13.129
important entitlements still have an accountable owner.

00:01:13.129 --> 00:01:16.880
Usability matters because controls that obstruct normal work can encourage unsafe

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:17.880
workarounds.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.250
A well-designed program makes the appropriate path understandable and efficient while

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:23.976
reserving additional friction for higher-risk decisions.

00:01:23.976 --> 00:01:26.720
Least privilege does not mean minimum access at any cost.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:31.360
It means access that is sufficient for the approved task, limited in scope and duration,

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:33.620
and supported by policy, monitoring, and review.
